SAMN05991734	22.75 -158	"Pacific Ocean: North Pacific Gyre, Station ALOHA"	1000	2011/12/20	-	-	-	-	-	34.482	-	-	-	3.78	-	-	marine metagenome : HOT ALOHA metagenomic time and depth series	"A time-resolved deep metagenomic survey of bacterioplankton from the ocean- surface to a depth of 1,000- in the North Pacific Subtropical Gyre at Station ALOHA, collected from Hawaii Ocean Time-series (HOT) cruises from August 2010 through April 2016."	PRJNA352737	-	-	SRA491398	-	5991734	SAMN05991734	408172	marine metagenome	-	-	-	-	-	NextSeq 500	-	15420080216	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-
SAMN06240272	22.8 -46.05	Atlantic Ocean	4425	2011/11/8	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	1.5	-	-	sediment metagenome : sediment metagenome Metagenome	"Microbial metabolism in the oxic/anoxic transition zones (OATZ) of sediments can serve as a barrier preventing the emission of nutrients and greenhouse gases diffusing upwards to the overlying water column. However, microbial diversity and activities in this transition zone are not well understood. Here we propose to employ metagenomic shotgun DNA sequencing on three representative samples from oligotrophic sediment columns retrieved from North Pond during IODP Expedition 336. These sediments offer a unique opportunity to explore the OATZ in oligotrophic sediments, and are characterized by both an upper a lower OATZ. In short we aim at: elucidating the identity to the owners of functional genes that are not -ccounted-for in the 16S rRNA libraries. Investigate the genomic inventory of uncharacterized sedimentary lineages of putative archaeal ammonium oxidizers. Expand the current knowledge of the microbial community and its potential activity in the OATZ."	PRJNA341273	-	-	SRA528965	-	6240272	SAMN06240272	412755	marine sediment metagenome	-	-	-	-	-	Illumina HiSeq 1000	-	5665227880	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-
