SRR10294826	30.124051 N 42.120113 W	Atlantic Ocean:Lost City Hydrothermal Field	-	2005-08-01	2019-10-16T00:00:00.000	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	Illumina reads Lost City: sample LC_HO8_080105_Bio5slurp_B1	marine ultramafic hydrothermal vent biome	SRP225961	PRJNA577730	9210749	SRA980311	SRS5528823	13035994	SAMN13035994	652676	hydrothermal vent metagenome	-	marine hydrothermal vent chimney	-	-	-	Illumina HiSeq 2500	20465913721	45081024250	LC_HO8_080105_Bio5slurp_B1	WGS	METAGENOMIC	PCR	PAIRED	Genome sequencing and assembly	Environment	Genome	Whole	hydrothermal vent metagenome...:Lost City Hydrothermal Field	Environmental DNA sequencing of chimney rock collected at the Lost City hydrothermal vent field on the Mid-Atlantic Ridge. The vent field is fueled by chemical reactions between the ultramafic rock under the chimneys and ambient seawater. These serpentinization reactions provide reducing power (as hydrogen gas) and organic compounds that can serve as microbial food; the most abundant of these being methane and formate. Our results indicate that carbon metabolism in these Lost City chimney biofilms might depend on the utilization of formate by low-abundance Chloroflexi and Sulfurouvum species.
