SRR8503604	37.35361 N 0.286194 W	Spain: off the coast of Alicante	90m	15-Oct-2015	2019-01-29T00:00:00.000	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	Med-OCT2015-90m-7h marine metagenome	Med-OCT2015-90m-7h. Metagenome was obtained from the 5-0.22 micron fraction at 90m below sea surface, after a post-confinement of 7 hours on deck.	SRP092902	PRJNA352798	7182317	SRA841057	SRS4304995	10839330	SAMN10839330	408172	marine metagenome	seawater	-	marine biome	seawater	-	Illumina HiSeq 4000	8556003663	22576625476	Med-OCT2015-90m-7h	WGS	METAGENOMIC	RANDOM	PAIRED	Genome sequencing and assembly	Environment	Genome	Whole	marine metagenome...:Mediterranean Depth Profile Metagenomes	In the Mediterranean and other temperate waters, the stratification of the water column is a seasonal phenomenon that usually starts in April and ends in November. In this work, we have analyzed by high throughput metagenomics a fine profile of a stratified water column off the coast of Alicante, at 60 nautical miles, collected in October 2015. The bioproject contains several metagenomes and assembled genomes recovered from the same location but at different depths (15, 30, 45, 60, 75, 90, 1000 and 2000 m).
