DRR090569	44.0859 N 155.0153 E	Pacific Ocean	0 m	2014-07-25	2018-04-24T00:00:00.000	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	metagenome sequencing from 100pg DNA of S3-MR1404, using Nextera	North Pacific Ocean	DRP004188	PRJDB5681	5459104	DRA005726	DRS062136	8977569	SAMD00078383	408172	marine metagenome	sea water	-	oceanic epipelagic zone biome	marine pelagic zone	-	Illumina MiSeq	1274868985	2183009122	S3D3N	WGS	METAGENOMIC	RANDOM	PAIRED NOMINAL_LENGTH="500" NOMINAL_SDEV="150"	Metagenome	Environment	Genome	Whole	marine metagenome...:Library construction from subnanogram DNA for marine metagenomics	Shotgun metagenomic sequencing has been one of the indispensable techniques in environmental microbiology by the advancement of high-throughput sequencing technologies. However, limitation of sample volume, low biomass and/or the presence of high concentration of humic substances are issues for application of shotgun metagenomics for deep-sea environments such as bathypelagic to hadal waters, benthic habitats under oligotrophic oceans and subseafloor sediment. Here, we examined applicability of library construction kits based on adaptor ligation technique or tagmentation such as KAPA Hyper Prep Kit, Nextera XT DNA Library Preparation Kit and Ovation SP+ Ultralow Library Systems on shotgun metagenomic library for low amount of environmental DNA (0.1 to 1ng) from abyssal marine sediment, and compared microbial communities from the shotgun metagenomic libraries obtained by the three library construction kits.
