SRR5007139	37.35361 N 0.286194 W	Spain: off the coast of Alicante	90m	15-Oct-2015	2017-04-01T00:51:13.947	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	Med-OCT2015-90m	Med-OCT2015-90m metagenome was obtained from the 5-0.22 micron fraction at 90 m below sea surface. The sequencing was performed with an Illumina Hiseq 4000, 2x150bp.	SRP092902	PRJNA352798	3412813	SRA491632	SRS1791668	5992384	SAMN05992384	408172	marine metagenome	seawater	marine water	marine biome	seawater	-	Illumina HiSeq 4000	7545846783	18779280798	-	WGS	METAGENOMIC	RANDOM	PAIRED NOMINAL_LENGTH="150" NOMINAL_SDEV="0.0E0"	Genome sequencing and assembly	Environment	Genome	Whole	marine metagenome...:Mediterranean Depth Profile Metagenomes	In the Mediterranean and other temperate waters, the stratification of the water column is a seasonal phenomenon that usually starts in April and ends in November. In this work, we have analyzed by high throughput metagenomics a fine profile of a stratified water column off the coast of Alicante, at 60 nautical miles, collected in October 2015. The bioproject contains several metagenomes and assembled genomes recovered from the same location but at different depths (15, 30, 45, 60, 75, 90, 1000 and 2000 m).
