nitrogen, carbon, and sulfur cycling. Importantly, many of the most abundant and/or most active taxa were predicted aerobes, suggesting electron donor-based niche partitioning. This work provides an important biogeochemical map for multiple phyla, helping to resolve the impacts of hypoxia on nutrient flow in the dead zone.
