SRR8062317	10.617 N 65.167 W	Venezuela: Cariaco Basin	-	Nov-2014	2019-10-17T00:50:07.607	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	Metagenome of microbial communities: Cariaco Basin	-	SRP077602	PRJNA326482	6592269	SRA794743	SRS3938925	10231922	SAMN10231922	408172	marine metagenome	-	seawater	-	-	Niskin bottle	Illumina HiSeq 2500	10746153176	24755378774	D2b247B	WGS	METAGENOMIC	RANDOM	PAIRED	Other	Environment	Other	Other	marine metagenome...:Microbial Metagenome, Metatranscriptome &amp; Phylogenetic Libraries	Oxygen depleted water columns (ODWCs) appear to be expanding in response to global climate change. This alters trophic structure, compresses habitat and modifies geochemical cycles of major elements. Oxygen depletion can vary in intensity and duration from seasonal hypoxia to permanent anoxia. The focus of this study is a classic example of the anoxic end-member, the Cariaco Basin. The overall goal is to examine how microbial functional potential (metagenomic), activity (metatranscriptomic), taxonomic diversity (based on SSU rRNA) and the ecological/geochemical consequences (in terms of measured rates of key processes) relate along vertical oxygen/geochemical gradients and between seasons in the Cariaco Basin. This will reveal relationships between expression of particular sets of genes, environmental differences in nutrients, energy substrates and oxidant availabilities.
