SRR6660646	33.7891 N 118.6683 W	Pacific Ocean:Santa Monica Mounds	0-30 cm	2013-05-09	2018-01-29T00:00:00.000	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	Metagenomic sequencing of methane seep sediment from Santa Monica Mounds	Keywords: GSC:MIxS;MIMS:5.0	SRP131927	PRJNA431796	5035606	SRA654597	SRS2904179	8432486	SAMN08432486	412755	marine sediment metagenome	sediment	methane seep	ocean floor	cold seep	-	NextSeq 500	22664067390	49619974857	7142	WGS	METAGENOMIC	RANDOM	PAIRED	Genome sequencing and assembly	Environment	Genome	Whole	marine sediment metagenome...:A Genomic Atlas of Anaerobic Methanotrophic (ANME) Archaea	The anaerobic oxidation of methane is mediated by the syntrophic partnership of anaerobic methanotrophic (ANME) archaea and sulfate reducing bacteria (SRB). There are multiple clades of ANME that have yet to be cultured and to date few ANME species have been analyzed genomically. Here we used a combination of metagenomics and single cell sequencing to recover draft genomes from ANME-1, ANME-2a, ANME-2b, ANME-2c and ANME-3 clades to determine differences in their metabolisms with the goal to understand their niche partitioning in the environment.
