SRR12059192	56.62016667 N 11.670666669999946 E	Denmark	-	2013	2017-01-01T00:51:15.260	-	-	-	-	30.67	-	-	-	-	-	-	60B-13 Baltic marine sediment metagenome (37.3 mbsf) - raw reads	-	SRP068645	PRJNA308531	11163870	SRA1089301	SRS1254555	4395456	SAMN04395456	412755	marine sediment metagenome	-	Baltic marine sediment	-	-	-	Illumina HiSeq 2000	6789461671	10967164000	60B-13	WGS	METAGENOMIC	RANDOM	PAIRED	Metagenome	Environment	Genome	Whole	marine sediment metagenome...:Baltic marine sediment metagenome	Metagenomes were sequenced from sediment samples collected during the International Ocean Discovery Program Expedition 347, &quot;Baltic Sea Paleoenvironment&quot;. The sediments were retrieved from as far as 84.4 meters below the seafloor. They vary in age, organic carbon content, salinity, and other parameters that reflect the changing Baltic environment during the transition from the last ice age and throughout the Holocene. The Baltic Sea environment has a very dynamic history, having transitioned from a period of freshwater and low organic carbon deposition during the last glaciation to the modern Holocene period of brackish-marine water and high organic carbon. These climatic changes are reflected in the sediment record, and IODP 347 in 2013 was the first-ever scientific drilling expedition to the Baltic to retrieve high-resolution sediment cores documenting this history. The Baltic Sea is thus an excellent natural laboratory for understanding how microbial communities may shift in response to changing conditions in the deep subsurface.
