SRR8557215	24.54544 N 81.406150 W	USA: Florida Keys	-	May-2015	2019-03-12T00:50:09.133	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	Shotgun metagenomic sequencing of coral reef seawater : reef depth	seawater samples were collected from reef depth	SRP185472	PRJNA517146	7249698	SRA848150	SRS4349610	10854669	SAMN10854669	1561972	seawater metagenome	-	benthic seawater	-	-	bottle	Illumina HiSeq 4000	3878503522	8568844302	8_FK22	WGS	METAGENOMIC	RANDOM	PAIRED	Raw sequence reads	Environment	Genome	Whole	seawater metagenome...:Microbial survey of coral reef seawater microbial communities from Cuba and the Florida Keys	This study was conducted to compare the microbial diversity and composition between the more protected reefs in Jardines de la Reina (Gardens of the Queen), Cuba and the more impacted reef-systems of Los Canarreos, Cuba and the Florida Keys, U.S.A. Seawater samples were generated by filtering 2 L of seawater onto filters, extracting the DNA, amplifying the V4 hypervariable region of the 16S ribosomal RNA gene, and constructing and sequencing the MiSeq library. The raw sequence reads are uploaded here. Reef depth seawater DNA was also harvested from select reef locations in Jardines de la Reina and the Florida Keys and sequenced with shotgun metagenomic sequencing.
