SRR6387564	21.092318 N 78.73354 W	Cuba: Caribbean sea: Jardines de la Reina Archipelago	-	Feb-2015	2018-03-15T00:00:00.000	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	-	WGS of coral reef seawater	seawater samples were collected from reef depth	SRP185472	PRJNA517146	4844185	SRA639904	SRS2767007	8181972	SAMN08181972	1561972	seawater metagenome	-	benthic seawater	-	-	bottle	Illumina HiSeq 4000	3682383201	8194548560	3_Cuba Metagenome GoQE	WGS	METAGENOMIC	RANDOM	PAIRED	Raw sequence reads	Environment	Genome	Whole	seawater metagenome...:Microbial survey of coral reef seawater microbial communities from Cuba and the Florida Keys	This study was conducted to compare the microbial diversity and composition between the more protected reefs in Jardines de la Reina (Gardens of the Queen), Cuba and the more impacted reef-systems of Los Canarreos, Cuba and the Florida Keys, U.S.A. Seawater samples were generated by filtering 2 L of seawater onto filters, extracting the DNA, amplifying the V4 hypervariable region of the 16S ribosomal RNA gene, and constructing and sequencing the MiSeq library. The raw sequence reads are uploaded here. Reef depth seawater DNA was also harvested from select reef locations in Jardines de la Reina and the Florida Keys and sequenced with shotgun metagenomic sequencing.
